   "intro": "A Lapras at the shore, singing softly. It looks at your Berry pouch, then at the water. A fisher's boy, Theo: \"It's been there a month. Every pod that passes, it sings. None stop.\" Theo: \"It's small for a Lapras. I think it's a baby.\"",
   "choices": [
    {
     "label": "Feed it.",
     "requires": [
      {
       "kind": "bagHas",
       "ids": [],
       "count": 1,
       "suffix": "-berry",
       "label": "a Berry"
      }
     ],
     "success": {
      "text": "It eats from your hand, slowly, like it forgot how. Then it nuzzles you, hard enough to knock you a step back, and sings one soft note just for you.",
      "effects": [
       {
        "kind": "spendBag",
        "ids": [],
        "count": 1,
        "suffix": "-berry"
       },
       {
        "kind": "friendship",
        "bond": 1,
        "who": "party"
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "label": "Ride it out to look for the pod.",
     "success": {
      "text": "You climb onto its shell. It is warm. It looks back at you once, and swims out into the grey.",
      "effects": [
       {
        "kind": "addEvent",
        "eventId": "lapras-sea-1"
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "label": "Ask Theo what else he knows.",
     "success": {
      "text": "Theo lowers his voice. Theo: \"Some men with nets came through. Before it showed up.\" He looks out at the water. \"I don't think it got lost.\"",
